  <h1>Ignite</h1>
  <p>Ignite is an admin panel for <a target="_new" rel="noopener" href="https://rocket.rs">Rocket</a>, the Rust web framework. Give it a MariaDB or MySQL table and it builds a back office for that table: a login page, a dashboard, and screens to list, search, sort, create, edit and delete its rows.</p>
  <p><strong>Status.</strong> Ignite is in development. The panel, the resources, the derive, the dashboard with its stat cards and tables of the latest records, and the sign-in protections (server-side sessions, form tokens and login throttling), with the same token check on an app's own form routes, are built. Some features are not yet, such as filters and bulk actions. Each page on this site says what is built and what is not.</p>

  <h2>What Ignite is</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A panel inside your app.</strong> It mounts in a Rocket app, under <code>/admin</code> by default.</li>
    <li><strong>Modelled on Filament 5.x.</strong> It has a panel, resources, forms, tables, actions, notifications, widgets and a login. The pages here follow the Filament docs' order, so that reference is useful for the ideas.</li>
    <li><strong>Written in Rust.</strong> A resource is a Rust type that implements a trait, or one that <code>#[derive(IgniteResource)]</code> writes from an Orbit model. The resource names the table's fields and columns, and how to list, create, update and delete its rows. Ignite draws the screens from that.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What Ignite is not</h2>
  <p>Version 1 leaves these out:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Infolists, a read-only view of one record.</li>
    <li>Several panels and translations. The panel has a light and a dark theme, which each user switches with the button in the top bar.</li>
    <li>Relations between tables, file uploads, filters and bulk actions.</li>
    <li>Charts. The widgets are stat cards and tables of the newest records.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Ignite also supports MariaDB and MySQL only.</p>

  <h2>How it relates to Propel</h2>
  <p><a target="_new" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/lajennylove/Propel">Propel</a> renders Ignite's screens. The panel's views live in the <code>ignite</code> namespace, so an app can extend them with <code>@@extends('ignite::layouts.app')</code>. Debug builds render views at runtime. Release builds render compiled views.</p>

  <h2>How it relates to Orbit</h2>
  <p><a target="_new" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/lajennylove/Orbit">Orbit</a> is the ORM that queries the database. A resource's queries are Orbit queries, whether the derive writes them or you do. When the app's Rocket build ignites, the panel opens an Orbit connection pool of 10 connections to <code>DATABASE_URL</code>. The panel's routes are async and share that pool. A connection that fails stops the launch with an error.</p>
